@hostname = https://localhost:7058
@tenantId = 1
@baseUrl = {{hostname}}/tenant/{{tenantId}}
@tagSystem = https://example.org/ignixa/samples
@tagCode = semantic-search-http
@packageId = ignixa.sample.semantic-search
@packageVersion = 1.0.0

# Semantic (vector) search: rank Observations by meaning instead of exact token/string match.
# Reference: docs/site/docs/server/features/semantic-search.md and
# docs/features/semantic-search/adr-2610-semantic-vector-search.md
#
# Use a disposable test tenant, never tenant 0 or production. In single-tenant mode,
# set baseUrl to {{hostname}}. If authorization is enabled, add your Authorization header
# to every request; the admin package requests need an administrator principal.
#
# Prerequisites (the feature is off by default):
# 1. SQL-backed storage on Azure SQL Database or SQL Server 2025+ (native vector type, schema v4).
#    The FileSystem data layer is not supported and fails startup when the feature is enabled.
# 2. Embedding provider settings (Azure OpenAI), as appsettings or environment variables:
#      VectorSearch__Enabled=true
#      VectorSearch__Embedding__Endpoint=https://<resource>.openai.azure.com/
#      VectorSearch__Embedding__DeploymentName=<deployment of a 1536-dimension model>
#      VectorSearch__Embedding__ModelName=text-embedding-3-small
#    Authentication uses Managed Identity, or DefaultAzureCredential locally (for example `az login`).
#    Every write of a semantic-indexed resource and every semantic search calls the provider.
# 3. A SearchParameter carrying the vector-search-config extension, delivered as a FHIR package.
#    The sample package in ./data/semantic-search-package defines `semantic-text` on Observation.
#    The admin load endpoint fetches packages from the configured npm registry, so publish the
#    sample to a registry the server can reach, for example a local one:
#      cd docs/rest/data/semantic-search-package
#      npm pack                                          # produces ignixa.sample.semantic-search-1.0.0.tgz
#      npx verdaccio                                     # local registry, default http://localhost:4873
#      npm publish --registry http://localhost:4873
#    then start the server with PackageManagement__NpmRegistry__RegistryUrl=http://localhost:4873.
#    The package must be loaded BEFORE the seed requests: there is no backfill yet, so resources
#    written before the parameter exists are never embedded (follow-up #495).
#    Not verified against a local registry in CI. If step 4 fails, check the server log: the
#    registry must serve npm version metadata at {registry}/{packageId}/{version} and the
#    tarball URL must sit under the registry base.
#
# Run in order: 4 (load) -> 5 (confirm) -> 6 (seed) -> 7 onward (search). The embedding model
# decides exact scores, so the expected ordering below is qualitative.

### 4. Load the package that defines the semantic-text SearchParameter
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/packages/load
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "packageId": "{{packageId}}",
  "version": "{{packageVersion}}",
  "includeDependencies": false
}

### 4b. List packages loaded in the tenant (expect the sample package)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/packages

### 5. Confirm the parameter is advertised: Observation.searchParam "semantic-text" with type "special"
# If it is absent, the feature is disabled or the parameter was not activated.
GET {{baseUrl}}/metadata
Accept: application/fhir+json

### 6a. Seed: persistent cough
PUT {{baseUrl}}/Observation/semantic-http-cough
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

{
  "resourceType": "Observation",
  "id": "semantic-http-cough",
  "meta": { "tag": [{ "system": "{{tagSystem}}", "code": "{{tagCode}}" }] },
  "status": "final",
  "code": { "coding": [{ "system": "http://loinc.org", "code": "11506-3", "display": "Progress note" }] },
  "valueString": "Patient reports a persistent dry cough for the past two weeks, worse at night"
}

### 6b. Seed: chest tightness on exertion
PUT {{baseUrl}}/Observation/semantic-http-chest
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

{
  "resourceType": "Observation",
  "id": "semantic-http-chest",
  "meta": { "tag": [{ "system": "{{tagSystem}}", "code": "{{tagCode}}" }] },
  "status": "final",
  "code": { "coding": [{ "system": "http://loinc.org", "code": "11506-3", "display": "Progress note" }] },
  "valueString": "Complains of chest tightness and shortness of breath when climbing stairs"
}

### 6c. Seed: blood pressure (text lives in note.text, the second path of the expression)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/Observation/semantic-http-bp
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

{
  "resourceType": "Observation",
  "id": "semantic-http-bp",
  "meta": { "tag": [{ "system": "{{tagSystem}}", "code": "{{tagCode}}" }] },
  "status": "final",
  "code": { "coding": [{ "system": "http://loinc.org", "code": "11506-3", "display": "Progress note" }] },
  "note": [{ "text": "Elevated blood pressure noted during the visit; advised to reduce sodium intake" }]
}

### 6d. Seed: routine check-up, status preliminary (for the status filter example)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/Observation/semantic-http-routine
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

{
  "resourceType": "Observation",
  "id": "semantic-http-routine",
  "meta": { "tag": [{ "system": "{{tagSystem}}", "code": "{{tagCode}}" }] },
  "status": "preliminary",
  "code": { "coding": [{ "system": "http://loinc.org", "code": "11506-3", "display": "Progress note" }] },
  "valueString": "Routine annual check-up, no complaints, vitals within normal limits"
}

### 7. Semantic search. No keyword overlaps with the notes. Expect cough and chest tightness
# ranked above blood pressure and the routine visit, entries in descending
# Bundle.entry.search.score (range 0 to 1), each with search.mode "match".
# The value is sent verbatim: commas are not OR-split.
GET {{baseUrl}}/Observation?_tag={{tagCode}}&semantic-text=trouble%20breathing%20and%20coughing
Accept: application/fhir+json

### 8. Same query with strict handling, so an unknown or disabled parameter is a 400 instead of ignored
GET {{baseUrl}}/Observation?_tag={{tagCode}}&semantic-text=trouble%20breathing%20and%20coughing
Accept: application/fhir+json
Prefer: handling=strict

### 9. Semantic term intersected with an ordinary filter: only status=final rows are ranked
GET {{baseUrl}}/Observation?_tag={{tagCode}}&status=final&semantic-text=high%20blood%20pressure
Accept: application/fhir+json

### 10. Paging: offset-based; the query embedding is cached, so page 2 ranks by the same vector as page 1.
# Follow the Bundle link with relation "next" for the next page.
GET {{baseUrl}}/Observation?_tag={{tagCode}}&semantic-text=trouble%20breathing%20and%20coughing&_count=2
Accept: application/fhir+json

### 11. An explicit _sort takes priority over relevance; distance only breaks ties within the sort
GET {{baseUrl}}/Observation?_tag={{tagCode}}&semantic-text=trouble%20breathing%20and%20coughing&_sort=-_lastUpdated
Accept: application/fhir+json

### 12a. Rejected: modifiers are not defined for a semantic parameter (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/Observation?_tag={{tagCode}}&semantic-text:text=anything
Accept: application/fhir+json
Prefer: handling=strict

### 12b. Rejected: a chain cannot end in a semantic parameter (400, "Semantic search chains are not supported")
GET {{baseUrl}}/DiagnosticReport?result:Observation.semantic-text=anything
Accept: application/fhir+json
Prefer: handling=strict

### 12c. Rejected: the _has form of a semantic chain (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/Patient?_has:Observation:subject:semantic-text=anything
Accept: application/fhir+json
Prefer: handling=strict

### 13a. Delete a seeded Observation; its vectors are removed with it
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/Observation/semantic-http-cough

### 13b. Re-run request 7: the cough Observation must no longer appear
GET {{baseUrl}}/Observation?_tag={{tagCode}}&semantic-text=trouble%20breathing%20and%20coughing
Accept: application/fhir+json

### 14. Cleanup: delete the remaining seeded Observations (re-run the seed PUTs to start over)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/Observation/semantic-http-chest

###
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/Observation/semantic-http-bp

###
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/Observation/semantic-http-routine

# When the feature is disabled (VectorSearch__Enabled=false), the same semantic-text queries behave
# like an unknown parameter: ignored with an OperationOutcome warning by default, and 400 under
# "Prefer: handling=strict". Nothing calls the embedding provider.
#
# If a seed PUT returns 503, the embedding provider is unavailable: the write fails and nothing is
# committed. Semantic searches also call the provider (once per query, then cached), so they depend
# on it too.
